export anchor PostageStampsStyle:
    number: 118
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Postage stamps
    idea: The dashboard is a page in a stamp album, where numbers are denominations, projects are a perforated souvenir sheet with an overprinted status, and the chart is a coil of one task stamps.
    base: light
    palette:
        album: #f5f0e1, the page and the perforation holes
        quadrille: #e4dccb, the 12px album grid, decorative only
        gumPaper: #fffdf6, stamp faces and fields
        sheetMargin: #e9e1cc, the souvenir sheet selvage
        ink: #22201c, text, frames and the On track overprint
        muted: #5b5348, captions and meta
        carmine: #9e2b3a, the primary button, overdue, Behind and this week
        ultramarine: #2b3f8f, a stamp colour and focus
        bottleGreen: #24604a, a stamp colour
        sepia: #6b4523, a stamp colour
        violet: #5d3b7a, a stamp colour
        slate: #37505e, a stamp colour and last week
        cancel: #3a3a44, postmarks
    type:
        Three stacks. Caps is Copperplate, Copperplate Gothic Light,
        Engravers MT, Felix Titling, Didot, Georgia, serif, set in caps with
        0.1 to 0.16em tracking. Numbers are Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT,
        Big Caslon, Georgia, serif. Body is Baskerville, Baskerville Old
        Face, Libre Baskerville, Georgia, serif. Sizes are 52 to 56px Didone
        denominations, 36px Didone greeting, 11 to 15px engraved caps
        labels, 17px bold Baskerville stamp names and 15px body.
    layout:
        The page is an album leaf on a quadrille ground with a thin rule and
        a double outer rule. The header has the brand in spaced caps with a
        framed star mark and, on the right, the search, a carmine New
        project button with an inner white line, the bell and the italic
        user name. The navigation is a row of small perforated definitive
        stamps, each a line icon and a caps label in its own stamp colour,
        the current one filled carmine. The greeting and date sit left with
        a carmine overdue line, and a round postmark reading Brightwork, 31
        OCT, 2026 with wavy cancel lines sits right. Four perforated stamps
        show the figures as big Didone denominations with an engraved icon
        and a caps caption. The projects form a souvenir sheet on a tinted
        margin with italic selvage text, six stamps in three columns. Each
        stamp has Brightwork and the team in caps along the top, a hatched
        vignette with a line drawing for its team, the percent as the
        denomination, the name, tasks and due date, and a full width status
        overprint bar along the bottom. The chart is a coil of stacked
        blocks where one block is one task, slate last week and carmine this
        week. Activity sits beside it, each line with a round postmark for
        its time. The sheet goes two across below 1000px and one across
        below 640px.
    spacing: An 8px unit. A 9px perforated margin round every stamp, 16px between stamps and 36px before sections.
    density: Medium. Each project is one self contained stamp, read at a glance.
    corners: Square. Edges are perforated with holes on a 10px pitch cut into the margin.
    borders: A 2 to 3px frame in the stamp colour inside the perforations. The album leaf has a thin rule and a double outer rule.
    shadows: A 1px drop shadow so stamps lift off the album.
    icons:
        Engraved line vignettes per team. Overprint bars carry the status,
        a filled dot on black for On track, a triangle on a white bar with a
        dashed top for At risk and a square on carmine for Behind. A clock
        marks overdue.
    focus: A 3px ultramarine outline offset 4px.
    tone: Philatelic and calm, such as The project issue, Recent post and denomination.
